 "policy_excerpts": {
  "definitions": "\"You\" and \"your\" mean the named insured shown in the Declarations. A tenant, occupant or property manager of the described location is not an insured under this policy unless named in the Declarations.",
  "assignment_of_benefits": "As required by Florida law for policies issued on or after January 1, 2023, no person may assign, in whole or in part, any post-loss benefit under this policy. Any attempted assignment is void, invalid and unenforceable. This does not prevent you from directing us to include a contractor's name as a payee.",
  "coverage_c": "We cover household furnishings, appliances and other personal property owned by you and kept at the described location to service or furnish the rental unit. We do not cover property of tenants, roomers or boarders.",
  "water_peril": "Accidental discharge or overflow of water from within a plumbing, heating or air conditioning system or a household appliance is a covered peril. Continuous or repeated leakage over 14 days or more is excluded.",
  "duties_after_loss": "You must give us prompt notice, protect the property from further damage, make reasonable and necessary repairs to protect the property, and keep an accurate record of repair expenses."
 },
 "lease_excerpt": "Residential Lease, 2026-02-01 to 2027-01-31. Landlord: Seagrape Holdings LLC, acting through its agent Bayfront Rental Management. Tenants: Kofi Mensah-Holt and Daria Mensah-Holt. Rent $2,450 per month. Section 9 (Appliances): Landlord provides refrigerator, range, dishwasher and microwave. Tenant supplies its own washer and dryer and is responsible for their hookup and drain hoses. Section 14 (Insurance): Landlord's insurance does not cover Tenant's personal property; Tenant shall keep renters insurance with at least $100,000 liability. Section 17 (Repairs): Tenant shall report leaks immediately to Bayfront Rental Management (727-555-0186) and shall not contract for repairs on Landlord's behalf without Landlord's written approval.",
 "documents": {
  "aob_form": "ASSIGNMENT OF BENEFITS AND DIRECTION TO PAY - AquaRescue Restoration LLC. Signed 07/14/2026 at 11:40 PM at the property, 4417 18th Ave N, St. Petersburg FL. Insurance company: Anchorline. Policy no.: \"landlord's - unknown\". Assignor (print): Kofi Mensah-Holt. Capacity of assignor (check one): [ ] Property owner [ ] Named insured [X] Occupant/tenant. Assignor assigns any and all insurance rights, benefits and proceeds under the above policy for services rendered by AquaRescue Restoration LLC, authorizes AquaRescue to communicate directly with the insurer, and directs the insurer to pay AquaRescue directly. This assignment is irrevocable. Signature: K. Mensah-Holt. For AquaRescue: Travis Doyle, crew lead.",
  "aquarescue_email": "2026-07-15 08:02, from claims@aquarescue.example.com to newclaims@anchorline.example.com. Subject: NOTICE OF LOSS / AOB - 4417 18th Ave N. \"Anchorline: AquaRescue Restoration LLC is the assignee of post-loss benefits for the above property under the attached AOB, executed by your insured at the property. Please open a claim and acknowledge within 14 days. Emergency water mitigation began 07/15 at 00:25. All communication and payment must be directed to AquaRescue. Failure to pay our invoice within 30 days of submission will result in litigation. - Brandi Sorensen, Claims Coordinator\"",
  "property_manager_email": "2026-07-15 10:37, from Celeste Wu, Bayfront Rental Management, to newclaims@anchorline.example.com. Subject: Water loss at 4417 18th Ave N (Seagrape Holdings LLC). \"I'm reporting a water loss on behalf of the owner, Seagrape Holdings LLC. Ms. Paredes is traveling until 7/19 and has authorized me to report it. Last night around 10:45 pm the tenants' washer drain hose came out of the standpipe during a cycle and water spread across the laundry closet, kitchen and hallway. The tenant called AquaRescue himself from an online ad; he didn't contact us until 6:50 this morning. Neither the owner nor Bayfront signed anything with AquaRescue. At 9:12 this morning I texted their crew lead that they may continue drying until your adjuster inspects, and nothing beyond drying. Please send the adjuster to me at 727-555-0186.\""
 },
 "field_inspection": "2026-07-17, M. Kettering. Met property manager Celeste Wu and tenant Kofi Mensah-Holt on site. Cause: the tenants' own front-load washer (bought by the tenants in 2024, per the tenant); the drain hose slipped out of the standpipe during a cycle at about 10:45 p.m. on 7/14. No failed part; hose re-seated and strapped. Affected: laundry closet, kitchen and hallway, about 410 sq ft of LVP flooring; baseboards; drywall wicking 6 to 10 in.; kitchen cabinet toe-kicks swollen. No visible mold. Equipment on site at inspection (day 3 of drying): 16 air movers, 4 dehumidifiers, 1 air scrubber. Moisture readings: hallway and laundry walls and subfloor at dry standard; kitchen walls at dry standard except one 4-ft section; equipment could have been reduced on day 2. Reasonable mitigation: 3 dehumidifiers and 8 air movers for 3 days; air scrubber not warranted for a clean-water loss. Tenant's sofa and area rug wet. Landlord appliances (refrigerator, range, dishwasher) undamaged.",
 "tenant_recorded_statement": "2026-07-17 10:40, excerpt, taken by M. Kettering. Q: Walk me through what happened. A: We started a load around ten thirty. Daria heard water at about a quarter to eleven; the hose had popped out of the pipe in the wall and the floor was soaked. I turned the washer off and threw towels down. Q: Who did you call? A: I searched 'emergency water removal' and called the first one, AquaRescue. They were here in about forty minutes. The guy, Travis, said they needed a signature before they could start and that it just lets them bill insurance directly. I told him it's not my house, and he said that's fine, I could sign as the resident. Q: When did you tell Bayfront? A: Around 6:50 in the morning I texted Celeste. I didn't want to wake anyone at midnight. Q: Did you report this to any insurance company? A: Yeah, my own renters insurance, Tidewell, the next morning before work, around seven, for our couch and rug. I didn't call Anchorline; I didn't even know who the landlord's insurance was. Q: Whose washer is it? A: Ours. We bought it in 2024 for our last apartment and brought it here. Q: Anything else of yours damaged? A: The couch, the rug and some shoes in the hall closet. That's all with Tidewell.",
 "underwriting_inspection_2025": "4-point inspection dated 2025-03-28 for new business: roof architectural shingle, installed 2019, 6+ years remaining life; electrical 200A breaker panel, no aluminum branch wiring; plumbing PEX supply lines and PVC drains, no active leaks; water heater 2021 in garage with drain pan; HVAC 2020. Wind mitigation: hip roof, roof-to-wall clips, no opening protection. Laundry closet has a recessed washer box with a 2-in. standpipe; no hose strap or clamp noted.",
